              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MAGGIE MCGUIRE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful flavor combination, Darien! Just like the Italian Sodas I get from my favorite espresso shop!I never would have thought to combine these two flavors. Yummy! Thanks."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CCURCIO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What am I doing wrong? Why does the half and half get all clumpy? I made again without half and half and it tasted great, but I wanted the creaminess in it.",
            "datePublished": "2004-07-22T12:55:20.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kidacat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love these. They are so refreshing. I found syrup at Whole Foods that doesn't have High Fructose Corn Syrup. I use 0.5 oz heavy whipping cream instead of half and half and I think it tastes much better. This is a much better than some of those high calorie drinks from Starbucks and much more refreshing.",
            "datePublished": "2009-05-30T21:40:13.597Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "momof3boys"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Thanks for reminding me of this great drink. I enjoy this with many different flavored syrups. For those with curdling issues...try mixing the syrup and cream then adding the soda water. It doesn't look as pretty but my cream didn't curdle any more.",
            "datePublished": "2008-03-30T19:32:24.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lynnette Isaacson Thorne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love Italian sodas! I used this recipe as a base but with different flavors. I have used milk as I don't always have cream handy and I add a bit more than this recipe calls for.\n\nFor those having problems with curdling, I read somewhere that if you put the syrup in the glass first, then the milk/cream, stir. Then add the ice and finally the carbonated/soda water. Not sure if that works all the time, but it does for me. :)",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-30T00:11:33.790Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KMack1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made one of these with raspberry flavored syrup for 'dessert' tonight - it's great with orange, too!",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-20T20:21:51.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jasmine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am excited to make this recipe but I saw a lot of reviews on curdling it is very important that you put the cream in last to prevent curdling and to stir right before drinking.",
            "datePublished": "2008-05-28T07:56:12.893Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Julie Olsen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My sons love Italian Sodas, so we decided to make them ourselves. We used Raspberry and Vanilla flavoring. The drinks were fabulous! Will make again and again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-23T13:54:27.047Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "flutebabe"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was paying for these at our favorite restaurant then decided I could have any flavor I wanted at home for a fraction of the price...They are so refreshing and delicious. My favorite flavor is vanilla and my husbands is raspberry.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-24T06:18:11.637Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HotHam1584"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made these many many times. As I used to be a barista and had to make these. To avoid the curdling, make sure your seltzer water is also cold. Also it may not look as pretty, but try it this way: ice, syrup, seltzer water, cream. The colder the ingredients are, the less likely the cream will curdle.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-11T22:59:37.511Z"
          },
          {
